== the closure Xbar in P^1 x P^1 x P^1 ==
  Xbar is a divisor of tridegree (3,3,3); K_{(P^1)^3} = O(-2,-2,-2), so by
  adjunction K_Xbar = O(1,1,1)|_Xbar, which is AMPLE.  Hence Xbar is a
  minimal surface of GENERAL TYPE with
     p_g = h^0(O(1,1,1)) = 8,   K^2 = (H1+H2+H3)^2*(3H1+3H2+3H3) = 18.
  Sing(Xbar) is 0-dimensional (computed above), so the resolution is still
  of general type: by Bombieri-Lang the rational points of X are expected to
  lie on finitely many curves.
